  "slug": "go-sign-count",
  "title": "Count the signs",
  "kind": "code",
  "language": "go",
  "level": 1,
  "statement": "Read a list of integers and count how many are positive, negative and zero.\n\nInput: the first line holds n (0 <= n <= 1000). The second line holds n integers separated by spaces, each between -1000000000 and 1000000000 (the line is empty when n = 0).\n\nOutput: one line with three integers separated by single spaces: the number of positive values, the number of negative values and the number of zeros.\n\nExample\nInput:\n6\n3 -1 0 7 -5 0\nOutput:\n2 2 2",
  "starter_code": "package main\n\nimport (\n\t\"bufio\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n)\n\nfunc main() {\n\treader := bufio.NewReader(os.Stdin)\n\tvar n int\n\tfmt.Fscan(reader, &n)\n\tfor i := 0; i < n; i++ {\n\t\tvar x int\n\t\tfmt.Fscan(reader, &x)\n\t\t// Count x here\n\t}\n\t// Print: positives negatives zeros\n}\n",
  "time_limit_ms": 2000,
  "memory_limit_mb": 256,
  "comparator": "trim",
  "timer_seconds": 600,
